          "english_quote": "For some of the many things said are bound to turn out.",
          "issue": "Bare “turn out” does not clearly convey the contextual sense of ἀποβαίνειν: some predictions necessarily come about. In modern English, “turn out” ordinarily needs a complement indicating the result.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “For some of the many things said are bound to come about.” This proposed wording requires fresh review.",
